    "intro_narrative": "The H.M.S. Aetherius drifts silently through the clouds, its engines cold and its halls echoing with the groans of settling metal. As the Chief Artificer, you stand before the Main Engineering Console, surrounded by a maze of brass pipes, ticking gears, and steam valves. The ship's central cogitation engine has seized up due to corrupted data in the command buffer, leaving the vessel vulnerable to the turbulent skies. To restart the heart of the ship, you must manually route the steam pressure and logic flows through the backup auxiliary systems. The air is thick with the smell of ozone and grease. You must align the mechanical calculators, verify the pressure gauges, and decrypt the startup sequence before the pressure in the boiler reaches critical mass.",
    "narrative_style": "steampunk"
